==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{m|ang|ġe-}} + {{m|ang|*rof||an array, number, host}} (attested only in compounds: {{m|ang|secgrōf||host of men}}, {{m|ang|stæfrōf||alphabet}}). Cognate to {{cog|gml|grēve}} ({{cog|da|greve}}, {{cog|sv|greve}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ang|/jeˈreːfa/}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|head=ġerēfa|m|ġerēfan}}

# a [[reeve]] or official with local jurisdiction under the king; the chief magistrate of a district

